joe@ll.mit.edu (Joe Finnivan) writes:
: I just got the source code for nethack and built it for a SUN SPARC2 running
: X Windows.  I have been playing nethack on a PC for a while and have gotten
: used to using the cursor keys to move around the dungeon.  On the SPARC2 I
: have to use the hjkl keys to move around.  Since I use both machines on a
: regular basis, my brain has started to twist around at impossible angles
: trying to adapt.  If anyone knows how to tell nethack to use the SPARC2 cursor
: keys instead of hjkl, my brain will be grateful and I can go on to lead a
: normal (?) life again.

 Try setting the environment variable NETHACKOPTIONS to "number_pad"! This will
allow you to use the numeric keypad for movement.

